# hermes-9router-stb-installer — config/Caddyfile.template
#
# install.sh substitutes __DOMAIN__ with the value you provide via
# --with-proxy=<domain> and writes the result to config/Caddyfile.
# Caddy handles automatic HTTPS (Let's Encrypt) for a real domain name;
# for a bare IP or .local/.home.arpa name it falls back to a self-signed cert.
#
# SECURITY NOTE: this exposes the 9Router dashboard, which holds your
# provider API keys, to whatever network can reach __DOMAIN__. Make sure
# INITIAL_PASSWORD in .env has been changed from the default before using
# this, and prefer restricting access at your router/firewall to trusted
# networks or a VPN rather than the open internet if at all possible.

__DOMAIN__ {
	reverse_proxy /* localhost:20128
}

# Uncomment if you also enabled the Hermes dashboard (HERMES_DASHBOARD=1
# in .env) and want it reachable through the same proxy on a subpath.
# Verify this matches Hermes's current dashboard auth requirements in
# website/docs/user-guide/docker.md before relying on it — a non-loopback
# bind requires a configured DashboardAuthProvider (basic auth/OAuth/OIDC).
#
# __DOMAIN__/hermes/* {
# 	uri strip_prefix /hermes
# 	reverse_proxy localhost:9119
# }
